From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:05:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): render chat link rules and edit them in Settings

Short references in chat messages (BST-2135, #123, session:<id>) are plain
text today. This renders the user's link rules from /v1/link-rules and adds a
Settings group to edit them.

- web/src/lib/linkRules.ts checks and compiles a rule with the same checks as
  the server, so a rule that slipped past it still can't run, and links text
  through a remark pass after item labels have become chips. Like item
  labels, it never rewrites links (file links included), inline code, code
  blocks or raw HTML, and it applies to agent and user messages. Compiled
  regexes take their leading boundary as a group instead of lookbehind, which
  older Safari can't parse. Captures are percent-encoded and every href is
  re-parsed as http(s) before use.
- GitHub references link on the session's own provider host, read from the
  git info the PR panel already fetches; the runner's GitHub resource now
  reports the repository URL so a session with no PR knows its host. #N goes
  to /pull/N for a known PR and /issues/N otherwise.
- session:<id>[/<message id>] opens /c/<id>?message=<message id> in the app,
  the deep link item labels use for Show in conversation.
- Settings > General > Chat links lists, adds, edits, toggles, deletes and
  resets rules, shows each rule's error, and previews sample text with the
  rules being edited.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/chat-link-rules; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
